hint: Write the row down after each pass.
right: `[1, 5, 14, 28, 42, 42]`. Each update reads a value already changed in the same pass, so the row mixes two rows of the triangle. Going right to left keeps the left neighbour from the previous row.
wrong: Pass 1: [1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0]. Pass 2: [1, 2, 2, 0, 0, 0]. Pass 3: [1, 3, 5, 5, 0, 0]. Pass 4: [1, 4, 9, 14, 14, 0]. Pass 5: [1, 5, 14, 28, 42, 42].

=== task: predict hard
title: Which entry is the answer?
prompt: `run[i]` is the length of the run of increasing neighbours that ends at index i. What does it print?
code:
